  "step_3": "The decision reason emphasizes losses over gains and prefers the lottery with the more favorable maximum loss. The individual explicitly identifies the 3000 Euro potential loss in Lottery B (vs. no loss in Lottery A) and treats this loss as a critical factor in their decision, even though it occurs with only 20% probability. The information considered by the individual (the 3000 Euro loss risk in B) matches the information relevant to the decision reason. Furthermore, their justification—giving strong weight to the potential loss and choosing the safer option to avoid it—aligns with the rule of the decision reason, which prioritizes loss avoidance. Although the report does not use the exact terminology of the reason, the cognitive process described closely mirrors the logic of loss prioritization. Therefore, it is highly likely that the individual applied this decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 95
}

